{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>הבל.</b> It refers to the vanities of the world. He attached הבל to הבלים. And if one will not find among the nouns that are in the pattern of ארץ that change except for חדר משכבך וסגור דלתך מספח חמתך — these too are with patach, while this one is with tzere. The construct of singular to plural in a single matter goes in two ways: for greatness, like מלך מלכים, and the opposite, like עבד עבדים; הבל הבלים is like it. As in the matter of אך הבל בני אדם כזב בני איש במאזנים לעלות, המה מהבל יחד — and the mem is instead of יותר, like the mem of מכל שהיו לפני בירושלים, and the mem of מכל מלמדי השכלתי. The meaning is: if human beings were placed in the balance against הבל, they would be lighter than הבל. And the doubling of הבל הבלים is to indicate every time, as in the matter of נשאו נהרות יהוה נשאו נהרות קולם, and likewise סבוני גם סבבוני, many times. And lest a person say in his heart that there is הבל in the things of the world but there is in it a root that stands — behold, he has sealed everything [as] הבל."], :book :ecclesiastes, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {0 "The quoted phrases אך הבל...במאזנים לעלות and המה מהבל יחד conflate two verses (Psalms 62:10–11); translated as Ibn Ezra presents them, unified into a single citation. The 'mem is instead of יותר' refers to the comparative mem-prefix in מהבל (= 'more than הבל')."}, :source-witnesses [["Wikisource" "https://he.wikisource.org/wiki/%D7%90%D7%91%D7%9F_%D7%A2%D7%96%D7%A8%D7%90_%D7%A2%D7%9C_%D7%A7%D7%94%D7%9C%D7%AA"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:26:59.326107962Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}